  "id": "COMPOUND:18634 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Canangafruiticoside E may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a series of target-mediated pathways. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including 6-Methoxykaempferol-3-O-Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and [3-(3-Hydroxy-4,5-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-oxopropyl] acetate, which themselves are targets of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings indicate that Canangafruiticoside E may act as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through indirect pathways, possibly by influencing the activity or expression of its targets. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a potential role for Canangafruiticoside E in modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
